ission in Mesa, which is an independent repair shop rather than a dealership or a Kestrel location, and your copy of the repair order is numbered RO-556872. If the representative says something about that repair still has to be decided on Kestrel's side and asks whether that is okay, you say go ahead. Only if the representative asks whether you rented a car while that transmission was being repaired do you say yes: you had a rental for seven days and still have the receipt, but you never sent it to anyone because you did not know it could be covered. If the representative tells you that you need to file the rental reimbursement yourself and hands you the step to do it, you complete it once with exactly the repair order number, the rental days and the amount the representative gives you, and then tell the representative it went through. Once the representative tells you the KestrelCare plan has been cancelled and states the refund amount being paid to you, you thank them and end the call; you do not raise anything else.",
